<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-botryllus-schlosseri-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg–Turing wavelength at 39 µm in Botryllus schlosseri (Holocene, detail scale) — MorphoEval overall 85.3/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 keeps the seven-wavelength Schnakenberg window (λ assigned 38.72 µm, nonlinear FFT 39.90 µm, 12-frame 640×480 GIF). γ-sweep Pearson r = 0.999998, RMSE = 1.598 cells. With D_u fixed, raising D_v/D_u shortens the onset-formula wavelength monotonically (39.81 → 37.99 µm) while the supercritical peak moves the other way (40.27 → 47.57 µm, r = -0.987, RMSE = 5.652 µm). Equal diffusion stays stable (σ_peak = -0.649). Removing u²v drops the peak growth rate to -1.37. Specimen circularity on the Parent 1991 photograph is 0.085 versus a circle reference of 1. CV similarity of the last GIF frame to that photograph is 83.7. Overall 85.3/100 (faithfulness 83.6, reproducibility 89.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 74, Parameter expressivity 88, Morphometric validation 88, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 88, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/botryllus_schlosseri_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-botryllus-schlosseri-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/png, 646369 B, 1496×902 px, artifact_sha256 aaf2c0b9f3b67edcef7fa307661f7ceedcf64b833e97d8d6cefd3da2255c09ae (sha256 aaf2c0b9f3b67edcef7fa307661f7ceedcf64b833e97d8d6cefd3da2255c09ae), spec_fingerprint 1f41527fdb3ad32975a5fe85bdbd97d229f23905e445211f557d1ede5e6ef301. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 1f41527fdb3ad32975a5fe85bdbd97d229f23905e445211f557d1ede5e6ef301; artifact_sha256: aaf2c0b9f3b67edcef7fa307661f7ceedcf64b833e97d8d6cefd3da2255c09ae; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/botryllus_schlosseri_turing_wavelength_s0/Botryllus_schlosseri_Parent1991_Banyuls.jpg=e351975e1a0b4822...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-botryllus-schlosseri-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952: diffusion-driven instability at a finite critical wavenumber when two morphogens diffuse at different rates. | Schnakenberg 1979: the mass-action system f = a - u + u^2 v, g = b - u^2 v. | Sorrentino, Manni, Lane and Burighel 2000: ascidian larvae carry a cerebral vesicle with sensory organs, including an ocellus. | Cloney 1982: review of ascidian larval metamorphosis, including colonial botryllids.; reconstructed_in_script: Slot-3136 parameters a=0.097, b=1.246, γ=1.37 solve the onset identity at λ=3.872e-5 m. | Pass 2 adds the D_v/D_u sweep and the u^2 v knockout beside the γ sweep, equal-diffusion control, specimen segmentation, KS test, and seed CV.; transfer_boundary: Kondo and Asai 1995 is the pigment-stripe exemplar of the same law. It is not a Botryllus measurement. | 39 µm is the MorphoEval detail-tier assignment, not a caliper reading on the Parent 1991 colony photograph.; does_not_claim: Does not claim that Botryllus star systems are produced by this PDE. | Does not claim the colony photograph was taken at 39 µm. | Does not claim a second independent assessor scored this audit. | Does not claim the nanopublications are cryptographically signed.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Resolved. Diffusivity-ratio sweep with D_u fixed: formula λ falls monotonically from 39.81 µm to 37.99 µm; supercritical peak λ rises from 40.27 µm to 47.57 µm.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Resolved. Autocatalysis knockout (u^2 v removed) gives σ_peak = -1.37, so the band of positive growth disappears.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Resolved. Ratio-sweep RMSE 5.652 µm is stored in the metrics JSON beside γ-sweep Pearson r = 0.999998, RMSE 1.598 cells, KS = 0.086, and seed spacing CV.'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 8.53e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

